.TH "GCMallocRaw" "3" "2026\-11\-05" "GCmalloc"
.SH NAME
\fBGCMallocRaw\fR \- allocate memory via GC\&.
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function like \fBGCMalloc\fR(3) but not register pointer
to GC roots\&. This mean that when GC will be collect garbage,
pointer will be deleted if pointer not linked to other pointer\&.
Also no need free pointer\&.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return value is like \fBmalloc\fR(3)
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS 4
/* typedef struct User {\&.\&.\&.} User; \&.\&.\&. */
User* parent = (User*)GCMalloc(sizeof(User));
User* child = (User*)GCMallocRaw(sizeof(User));
if (!parent || !child) {
  /* \&.\&.\&. */
}

/* need to link child to parent */
GCAddDependency(parent, child);

/* Using special macro: */
GC_SET_PTR(parent, child, child);
